# agent: claude — changed 2026-08-05: the rule "content/3.api/" is gone.
#
# scripts/ingest-exdoc.mjs writes those pages from ../doc, the ExDoc
# output, thus they are generated files and the first instinct is to
# ignore them. We commit them, because the machine that builds the site
# cannot make them: Vercel and GitHub Actions have Node, not Elixir, so
# `mix docs` never runs there and ../doc never exists.
#
# The script already expects this. When it finds no ../doc but finds
# content/3.api, it keeps the pages and warns; when it finds neither, it
# stops the build. Ignoring the pages therefore broke every build on a
# machine without Elixir.
#
# The cost is diff noise: `mix docs && pnpm ingest` after a docstring
# change shows the regenerated pages in the commit. That is the price of
# a reference that the site can always show.

# Vercel project link
.vercel
.env*
